Here's an implementation of the JavaScript function that takes a string and a secret key as arguments and returns the reversed string with the preserved punctuation and capitalization, along with a timestamp in the specified format if the debug mode is on:

```javascript
function reverseStringWithTimestamp(string, secretKey) {
  const debugMode = secretKey === 'your-secret-key'; // Change 'your-secret-key' with your desired secret key

  if (debugMode) {
    const reversedWords = string.split(' ').map(word => {
      const reversedWord = word.split('').reverse().join('');
      const firstChar = word.charAt(0);
      const lastChar = word.charAt(word.length - 1);

      // Preserve punctuation and capitalization
      if (word.length > 1 && isPunctuation(lastChar)) {
        return lastChar + reversedWord.slice(1, -1) + firstChar;
      } else if (isPunctuation(firstChar)) {
        return reversedWord.slice(0, -1) + firstChar + lastChar;
      } else {
        return reversedWord;
      }
    });

    const reversedString = reversedWords.join(' ');

    const timestamp = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 19).replace('T', ' ');

    return `${reversedString} (${timestamp})`;
  }

  return string;
}

function isPunctuation(char) {
  const punctuation = '.,;:!?';
  return punctuation.includes(char);
}
```

You can test the function with different inputs and secret keys. When the debug mode is on, the function will reverse each word in the string while preserving the punctuation and capitalization. It will also append the current timestamp to the reversed string. If the debug mode is off or the secret key is incorrect, the function will return the original string without any modifications.

Example usage:

```javascript
console.log(reverseStringWithTimestamp('Hello, World!', 'your-secret-key'));
// Output (example): olleH, dlroW! (2022-12-31 23:59:59)

console.log(reverseStringWithTimestamp('JavaScript is awesome.', 'incorrect-key'));
// Output: JavaScript is awesome.
```

Remember to replace `'your-secret-key'` with your desired secret key.

