The bug in the initial code was that the "flag" variable was not being reset to "true" at the start of each outer loop iteration. This caused the algorithm to exit prematurely, assuming the array was sorted even if there were further iterations required. By resetting the "flag" variable to "true" at the beginning of each iteration, we ensure that the algorithm accurately detects whether the array is already sorted or not.

Additionally, the comparison condition inside the inner loop has been changed to "array[j] < array[j + 1]" instead of "array[j] > array[j + 1]". This change ensures that the sorting is done in descending order.

Now, the algorithm will correctly perform bubble sort in descending order and accurately detect if the array is already sorted before completion.

