```

The logical error in the above code is that it simply calculates the sum of all the digits in the credit card number without following the Luhn algorithm. In the Luhn algorithm, every second digit (starting from the rightmost digit) needs to be doubled and, if the result is greater than 9, the digits of the result are summed. The erroneous code does not take this into account and sums all the digits directly, leading to incorrect validation results.
